From 814a307baefc72102e3ff9e2641811f0f093187a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:38:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] vulkan: sparse binds wait on the GPU, through the next
 submission

Every vkQueueBindSparse (zero block, tiles, layers) waited for a fence on
the CPU, stalling the GPU thread until the graphics queue drained: ~33 ms
per bind in Mario Kart World's terrain streaming. The bind now signals a
semaphore that the scheduler attaches, at every stage, to the next batch
it submits, whatever submits it. That batch holds the clear or the uploads
recorded after the bind, also when a staging request or anything else
flushes before the uploads are all recorded (a semaphore waited on only by
an explicit flush after the uploads would miss that case). The semaphore
is kept until its batch completes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
